In article <2093@isgtec.UUCP> ken@isgtec.UUCP (Ken Newman) writes:
>
>
>A simple question - is there any way to have your cat/dog NOT attack
>peaceful creatures? He seems to attack just about anything. Last game
>my cat started chewing on some hobbits, so they killed him. I'm assuming
>peaceful creatures really have uses, and it is worthwhile not to just
>pound them.
>- kn

Firstly as long as you do not kill the peaceful creatures you are alright.  If
you do , you lose luck  (50% of  the time) ,  as well  as a chance to loose an
intrinsic (very slight as I remember). But by far the easiest way to stop your
pet attacking peaceful  creatures is to leave it when going down the stairs or
kill  it ,  beacuse you may  lose luck initially  , but the  pet does not keep
getting in your way.

